# (after 0537) gl, vk: the GL and Vulkan layers' shaders from Metal SOURCE: <DM_MSL_DIR>/<api>/msl/<name>.metal, one library per function, compiled on the device at first use
#
# Origin:  written in this repository (the OpenGL / Vulkan games on the iPhone). No upstream commit: upstream's layers load only <api>_shaders.metallib, which the Mac's
#          gl_shaders.py / vk_shaders.py link (`xcrun metal`). Applies after 0537 (patch -p1).
# Licence: the licence of the tree it patches (the engine's MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds and contributors).
#
# Why: the iPhone has no `xcrun metal`, so it cannot make a metallib. A game whose GL or Vulkan shaders were translated on the phone (crates/ibuilder-glvk, the Rust port of
#   gl_shaders.py / vk_shaders.py, wired into stage 3 of the pipeline) ships Documents/shaders/<id>/{gl|vk}/<api>_shaders.tsv and msl/<name>.metal, one function per file (vk_<name>,
#   gl_<name>: the temporary .metal files the Python compiles one by one before it links the metallib). The layers found none of it: sh_load loaded the table, then logged
#   "[RED] shader library failed to open .../<api>_shaders.metallib", and every shader was "not in the library".
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/layer_msl.h (new), dm/gfx/vk/hle_vk.m, dm/gfx/gl/hle_gl.m; tests dm/gfx/tests/t_vk_msl_src.m, t_gl_msl_src.m):
#   * sh_load: when <DM_MSL_DIR>/<api>/<api>_shaders.metallib does not exist and <DM_MSL_DIR>/<api>/msl is a folder, the layer is in source mode (lmsl_probe): it logs one line
#     ("shaders from Metal source: <dir>/<name>.metal, ... engine-patches/0538 ...") and no [RED]. The order is: the metallib file, then msl/, then the RomFS trailer (as before).
#   * layer_fn(name): every function of the game's shader library is looked up through it: [g_lib newFunctionWithName:] when a metallib is loaded (as before), else lmsl_lib's library
#     of that name: <msl>/<name minus vk_ / gl_>.metal compiled with newLibraryWithSource, once, cached one library per name in a dictionary under a mutex (concurrent first uses may
#     compile twice; the first stored is kept); a missing file (a variant the tools did not make, vk_<key>_d) gives nil without a compile, as newFunctionWithName gives; a file that
#     does not compile is reported once with Metal's message ([RED], 50 lines at most per layer) and cached as failed. Only names of letters, digits and '_' after "<api>_" are read.
#     Sites: hle_vk.m vkCreateShaderModule (vk_<key>), spec_fn (layer_fn_cv: vk_<key>[_d] with its specialization constants), pipe_make (vk_<key>_d); hle_gl.m glCompileShader
#     (gl_<key>_v / gl_<key>_f). The layer's own shaders (host_msl_lib: gl_util's clr_vs / clr_fs, vk_fan) are not the game's library and are not changed. This tree's hle_vk.m has
#     no lookup of the viewport variants vk_<key>_vp<n> (upstream's newer layer has one): their files, when the tools write them, are not read here.
#   * Options: those of the NVN layer's source compiles (iOSBuilder's paches/0007 with engine-patches/0535): mathMode Relaxed, preserveInvariance YES, optimizationLevel Size, and
#     DM_MTL_OPT_SIZE=0 (dm_envflag.h, the switch 0535 reads; read once here too) gives the Default level. A plain [MTLCompileOptions new] with the three set: 0535 needs its
#     DmMslCompileOptions only because 0007's line cannot be edited from an engine patch, and its header says why a subclass cannot be used (MTLCompileOptions is a facade: an
#     instance of a true subclass has none of its properties). The Mac's tools compile with `metal -fpreserve-invariance -fwrapv` and the compiler's default fast math: -fwrapv has
#     no MTLCompileOptions counterpart.
#   * Teardown (the layers' session reset): the libraries go with the device (lmsl_teardown).
# Effect on games already built: none (a game with a metallib loads it as before). Compile cost: every function the game uses is compiled once per run from source at its
#   vkCreateShaderModule / glCompileShader (Metal's own compile cache serves the next runs); not measured on a phone.
# Games: the OpenGL (Digimon Story Cyber Sleuth, Balatro, ...) and Vulkan (Super Mario Galaxy, Super Mario 3D All-Stars, ...) games whose shaders were translated on the phone.
#   Switches: DM_MTL_OPT_SIZE (existing).
